[meat sizzling]

26
00:01:57.075 --> 00:01:58.700
[people chattering]

27
00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:03.498
[chill music playing]

28
00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:05.208
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

29
00:02:16.386 --> 00:02:20.723
[gentle music playing]

30
00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.778
- I'll catch up with you soon.
- [man 1] Quinn.

31
00:02:34.779 --> 00:02:37.781
- Well. if it isn't Staten Kirkland.
- In the flesh.

32
00:02:37.782 --> 00:02:40.034
- Better late than never.
- [man 2] Quinn.

33
00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:41.994
Staten.

34
00:02:44.038 --> 00:02:45.706
- Davis.
- Great party.

35
00:02:45.707 --> 00:02:48.459
What can I say? I'd do
anything for my nephew.

36
00:02:51.462 --> 00:02:53.214
Look at you. New dress.

37
00:02:53.882 --> 00:02:56.342
- No...
- Brings out the amber flecks in your eyes.

38
00:02:59.137 --> 00:03:00.346
Thank you.

39
00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:05.935
I'll leave you to it. I. uh... I got a
big birthday reveal in the works. so...

40
00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.148
[giggles]

41
00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:14.027
- "The amber flecks in your eyes"?
- He was just being nice.

42
00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:21.575
- It's good to see you out off the ranch.
- It's been a while.

43
00:03:21.576 --> 00:03:24.536
That's what the doctor
prescribes after your wife dies.

44
00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:28.791
Two years of heavy sulking. go
all-out shut-in. grow the beard out.

45
00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:30.460
[Quinn] I love it.

46
00:03:33.755 --> 00:03:35.505
Well. I mean. if you like it...

47
00:03:35.506 --> 00:03:38.092
might as well keep it. right?

48
00:03:39.969 --> 00:03:41.345
[girl laughs] Okay.

49
00:03:41.346 --> 00:03:44.014
Hey. hey. hey. hey. Shots
for the birthday boy.

50
00:03:44.015 --> 00:03:45.057
[boy] Ow!

51
00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:47.267
Always looking for trouble.

52
00:03:47.268 --> 00:03:50.437
Baby. I'm not looking for
trouble. I am trouble.

53
00:03:50.438 --> 00:03:51.981
[hushed] Reid. here he comes.

54
00:03:52.482 --> 00:03:53.733
Hey. Uncle Staten.

55
00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:55.818
Hey. boys. Lauren.

56
00:03:56.778 --> 00:03:58.071
Could I get a minute?

57
00:03:58.780 --> 00:03:59.821
- Yeah.
- [Lauren] Mm-hmm.

58
00:03:59.822 --> 00:04:00.822
Thanks.

59
00:04:06.287 --> 00:04:09.122
Where were you this morning?
I waited at the cliff for you.

60
00:04:09.123 --> 00:04:10.500
I never said I was coming.

61
00:04:11.668 --> 00:04:12.876
It's our tradition. Randall.

62
00:04:12.877 --> 00:04:14.503
- [car horn honks]
- [Reid] Randall!

63
00:04:14.504 --> 00:04:15.796
[engine revs]

64
00:04:15.797 --> 00:04:17.005
Hold... Hold...

65
00:04:17.006 --> 00:04:19.092
[pensive music plays]

66
00:04:21.844 --> 00:04:23.053
[Randall] Where are we going?

67
00:04:23.054 --> 00:04:24.388
[Reid] Trust me. trust me.

68
00:04:24.389 --> 00:04:25.514
[Randall laughs]

69
00:04:25.515 --> 00:04:27.057
- No way!
- Yes!

70
00:04:27.058 --> 00:04:28.309
- What?
- Yes!

71
00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.478
Uncle Davis!

72
00:04:31.145 --> 00:04:32.145
[Davis] Yeah.

73
00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:35.524
Come on. Dad! I told him
it was your favorite.

74
00:04:35.525 --> 00:04:36.525
[Randall] This is sick.

75
00:04:36.526 --> 00:04:40.738
Most of you knew my sister. I know
right now she's looking down on us.

76
00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:42.740
And she's. uh...

77
00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:45.368
She's saying. "Davey...

78
00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:49.080
you are spoiling that boy."

79
00:04:50.081 --> 00:04:50.998
As I should.

80
00:04:50.999 --> 00:04:52.040
[Randall laughs]

81
00:04:52.041 --> 00:04:55.294
- Happy birthday. Randall.
- Oh my God. Thank you. Uncle Davis.

82
00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:56.420
[guests clapping]

83
00:04:56.421 --> 00:04:57.463
[Davis] Enjoy.

84
00:05:05.847 --> 00:05:07.015
[woman] Let's go.

85
00:05:07.682 --> 00:05:09.642
[Staten] You're gonna
return that car first thing.

86
00:05:10.393 --> 00:05:12.894
People like Davis do not
give gifts without strings.

87
00:05:12.895 --> 00:05:14.604
What've you got against
Uncle Davis anyway?

88
00:05:14.605 --> 00:05:16.648
You act like you're the
only one who lost somebody.

89
00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:18.942
- Okay. I'm warning you...
- You're an asshole.

90
00:05:18.943 --> 00:05:21.988
- That is enough!
- God. I wish it was you that died.

91
00:05:25.908 --> 00:05:27.618
- Randall! Hey! R...
- [door slams]

92
00:05:42.925 --> 00:05:44.302
[phone vibrates]

93
00:05:54.645 --> 00:05:55.897
[Staten groans]

94
00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:03.196
Yeah. hello?

95
00:06:03.905 --> 00:06:06.406
[ominous tone surges]

96
00:06:06.407 --> 00:06:07.950
What are you talking about?

97
00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:11.079
[Staten exhales]

98
00:06:12.663 --> 00:06:13.663
[phone clatters]

99
00:06:13.664 --> 00:06:15.750
[Staten sobbing]

100
00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:24.384
[peaceful music playing]

101
00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:32.767
[woman] Hey. Quinn.

102
00:06:41.776 --> 00:06:42.944
Let's go. Biscuit.

103
00:06:50.118 --> 00:06:51.118
[door closes]

104
00:06:53.413 --> 00:06:55.415
[Biscuit pants. then yips]

105
00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:02.672
Sorry I'm late. Ellie. Tractor
died again. It's a whole thing.

106
00:07:03.214 --> 00:07:07.717
You realize how long it's gonna take me
to sow three acres of lavender by hand?

107
00:07:07.718 --> 00:07:10.638
Well. I hate to pile on. but
the Banjees just canceled.

108
00:07:13.224 --> 00:07:15.476
- But they're playing tonight.
- Not anymore they're not.

109
00:07:17.395 --> 00:07:18.353
[sighs]

110
00:07:18.354 --> 00:07:21.606
How am I supposed to run a dance hall
when the musical acts keep canceling?

111
00:07:21.607 --> 00:07:23.818
Well. I happen to
know a musician.

112
00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:26.653
- [laughing] No.
- Yes.

113
00:07:26.654 --> 00:07:27.988
- No.
- Why not?

114
00:07:27.989 --> 00:07:29.448
We both know the piano I play

115
00:07:29.449 --> 00:07:32.034
isn't the kind people around
here like to dance to.

116
00:07:33.703 --> 00:07:36.163
That and I'm meeting
Staten at the game tonight.

117
00:07:36.164 --> 00:07:37.873
And don't give me that look.

118
00:07:37.874 --> 00:07:38.874
What look?

119
00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:40.751
That look.

120
00:07:42.378 --> 00:07:44.629
Okay. I'm not giving any look.

121
00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:46.339
He's my friend. Ellie.

122
00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:48.468
You and Amalah were friends.

123
00:07:49.469 --> 00:07:52.596
It's not your job to put her
husband's heart back in one piece.

124
00:07:52.597 --> 00:07:54.390
And even if it were. Quinn.

125
00:07:55.516 --> 00:07:57.518
I'm not so sure
you could. I mean.

126
00:07:58.478 --> 00:07:59.770
not after Randall.

127
00:08:06.736 --> 00:08:07.569
[sighs]

128
00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:09.154
[crowd noises swelling]

129
00:08:09.155 --> 00:08:12.324
- [percussion playing]
- [crowd cheering]

130
00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:13.659
Let's go!

131
00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:16.203
Yeah. baby! Let's go!

132
00:08:16.204 --> 00:08:18.289
[marching band
playing lively music]

133
00:08:19.916 --> 00:08:22.001
[woman] Woo-hoo! Spartans!

134
00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:24.504
[girl] Go. Spartans!

135
00:08:26.589 --> 00:08:28.466
- That cherry soda for me?
- [Quinn laughs]

136
00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.552
Davis. No. it's not.

137
00:08:32.553 --> 00:08:33.470
[blows raspberry]

138
00:08:33.471 --> 00:08:35.764
- I am wounded. Yeah.
- Are you? Oh.

139
00:08:35.765 --> 00:08:37.766
It's all right. You
can make it up to me.

140
00:08:37.767 --> 00:08:39.726
- Can I?
- Mm. Dinner at Maeve's.

141
00:08:39.727 --> 00:08:41.979
[both laugh]

142
00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:44.105
Not exactly the reaction
I was hoping for.

143
00:08:44.106 --> 00:08:45.190
I'm sorry.

144
00:08:45.191 --> 00:08:47.817
It's just that you've had a
really long time to ask me that.

145
00:08:47.818 --> 00:08:49.277
You've heard of the friend zone?

146
00:08:49.278 --> 00:08:50.863
- Mm-hmm.
- That's right here.

147
00:08:51.489 --> 00:08:52.948
But way up here

148
00:08:52.949 --> 00:08:56.243
- is the brother of the best friend zone.
- Hmm.

149
00:08:56.244 --> 00:09:00.289
That one's real hard to shake off.
In fact. most men don't make it.

150
00:09:01.457 --> 00:09:02.832
You seem to think you have.

151
00:09:02.833 --> 00:09:04.961
Well. you know. Haven't I?

152
00:09:06.379 --> 00:09:09.214
- I don't know.
- Think about it. The offer stands.

153
00:09:09.215 --> 00:09:11.259
- I'm a real good time.
- Oh!

154
00:09:18.432 --> 00:09:21.060
[sentimental music plays]

155
00:09:22.645 --> 00:09:23.645
Hey.

156
00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:24.980
Hey.

157
00:09:27.024 --> 00:09:29.693
- I feel weird.
- Oh really? Couldn't tell.

158
00:09:29.694 --> 00:09:31.028
[laughing] Oh. piss off.

159
00:09:31.529 --> 00:09:32.362
[Quinn giggles]

160
00:09:32.363 --> 00:09:34.573
- Nachos?
- Oh. thank you.

161
00:09:34.574 --> 00:09:35.783
- Cherry soda?
- Oh!

162
00:09:36.909 --> 00:09:37.784
Thank you.

163
00:09:37.785 --> 00:09:39.912
- You're welcome.
- [marching band plays]

164
00:09:41.622 --> 00:09:43.624
[crowd cheering]

165
00:09:50.298 --> 00:09:51.716
[people whooping]I

166
00:09:56.053 --> 00:09:58.346
[crowd cheers and applauds]

167
00:09:58.347 --> 00:09:59.932
[exhales] Okay.

168
00:10:02.727 --> 00:10:04.478
Any sign of that UT scout?

169
00:10:05.855 --> 00:10:08.149
No. no one's ever
gonna come out here.

170
00:10:16.115 --> 00:10:19.243
[romantic music plays]

171
00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:29.378
Lucas Russell's
having a glow-up.

172
00:10:30.379 --> 00:10:32.130
Really? No. I did not notice.

173
00:10:32.131 --> 00:10:33.840
- [percussion plays]
- Okay. guys.

174
00:10:33.841 --> 00:10:35.258
- One on one. Ready!
- [team] Break!

175
00:10:35.259 --> 00:10:36.677
[players grunting]

176
00:10:38.721 --> 00:10:39.721
Come on.

177
00:10:39.722 --> 00:10:40.722
[grunts]

178
00:10:43.476 --> 00:10:45.061
Yes! Yes!

179
00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:47.604
Oh shit! [laughs]

180
00:10:47.605 --> 00:10:49.357
- Sorry.
- It's okay.

181
00:10:52.068 --> 00:10:53.360
[quarterback] Ready! Hut!

182
00:10:53.361 --> 00:10:54.612
[grunting]

183
00:10:57.948 --> 00:10:58.990
[grunts]

184
00:10:58.991 --> 00:11:00.409
[whistle blows]

185
00:11:04.622 --> 00:11:08.834
{\an8}[melancholy music playing]

186
00:11:10.544 --> 00:11:11.461
Hey.

187
00:11:11.462 --> 00:11:13.130
- You okay?
- Yeah.

188
00:11:14.382 --> 00:11:15.382
Yeah.

189
00:11:22.431 --> 00:11:25.642
- Let's get you out of here.
- No. no. no. I'm fine.

190
00:11:25.643 --> 00:11:27.727
I'm good. You stay.

191
00:11:27.728 --> 00:11:31.357
I'm gonna be by tomorrow to
look after that tractor. Okay.

192
00:11:37.279 --> 00:11:38.321
Hut!

193
00:11:38.322 --> 00:11:39.364
[players grunting]

194
00:11:39.365 --> 00:11:43.828
[stirring music playing]

195
00:11:44.787 --> 00:11:46.789
[crowd cheers]

196
00:11:56.924 --> 00:11:58.092
[brakes squeal]

197
00:11:59.218 --> 00:12:00.427
[engine shuts off]

198
00:12:00.428 --> 00:12:03.513
This isn't a good idea.
Lucas. We weren't invited.

199
00:12:03.514 --> 00:12:06.599
Yeah. we're never invited.
It's never a good idea.

200
00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:07.893
Come on. Jack.

201
00:12:09.603 --> 00:12:10.854
["Espresso" by Ryan Oakes plays]

202
00:12:10.855 --> 00:12:12.564
<i>♪ Every single hurdle
they try to fit in ♪</i>

203
00:12:12.565 --> 00:12:15.358
<i>♪ I clear them with a clear
conscience I'm never trippin' ♪</i>

204
00:12:15.359 --> 00:12:17.861
<i>♪ I had a bucket list until it
went and kicked the bucket ♪</i>

205
00:12:17.862 --> 00:12:20.447
<i>♪ I gave it up to move the
needle and it's barely budgin' ♪</i>

206
00:12:20.448 --> 00:12:23.116
<i>♪ It ain't no Biggie rhyme
We can try to up the budget ♪</i>

207
00:12:23.117 --> 00:12:25.702
<i>♪ But every time they pull the
strings I feel like I'm a puppet ♪</i>

208
00:12:25.703 --> 00:12:27.788
<i>♪ You're the
worst Go to work ♪</i>

209
00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:30.540
<i>♪ If you hurt Rub in dirt ♪</i>

210
00:12:30.541 --> 00:12:31.499
<i>♪ Why you mad? ♪</i>

211
00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:33.251
[indecipherable party chatter]

212
00:12:33.252 --> 00:12:34.545
<i>♪ Speed up ♪</i>

213
00:12:35.713 --> 00:12:37.965
<i>♪ Put it first Write a verse ♪</i>

214
00:12:38.716 --> 00:12:39.924
<i>♪ Reimburse ♪</i>

215
00:12:39.925 --> 00:12:43.595
What about "this is over" do you
not understand. Reid Collins?

216
00:12:43.596 --> 00:12:47.015
Babe. you said you wanted
space and I gave you space.

217
00:12:47.016 --> 00:12:49.768
- But it's gone on long enough. okay?
- I know.

218
00:12:49.769 --> 00:12:53.271
I just think we want
different things.

219
00:12:53.272 --> 00:12:54.314
- Hmm.
- Right?

220
00:12:54.315 --> 00:12:57.192
I want something that's...
more than this town.

221
00:12:57.193 --> 00:12:59.403
More isn't always
better. Lauren.

222
00:13:00.488 --> 00:13:03.448
You'll change your mind. You'll
see. You and me are meant to be.

223
00:13:03.449 --> 00:13:05.367
- [Reid laughs]
- [boys shouting]

224
00:13:15.419 --> 00:13:17.087
Ooh. Careful.

225
00:13:17.922 --> 00:13:19.173
That stuff will kill you.

226
00:13:19.757 --> 00:13:21.216
Consider my life saved.

227
00:13:21.217 --> 00:13:24.135
- Means you owe me a blood debt.
- A blood debt?

228
00:13:24.136 --> 00:13:25.262
Is that right?

229
00:13:25.846 --> 00:13:27.223
Now you gotta save me back.

230
00:13:28.474 --> 00:13:29.474
[laughs quietly]

231
00:13:36.524 --> 00:13:37.524
Deal's off.

232
00:13:40.319 --> 00:13:41.862
[lively music playing]

233
00:13:46.116 --> 00:13:49.035
You don't have to tell me this
town is sitting on liquid gold.

234
00:13:49.036 --> 00:13:51.496
I'm the one who pushed the
permits through city hall.

235
00:13:51.497 --> 00:13:53.122
[man] <i>We appreciate
that. Mr. Collins.</i>

236
00:13:53.123 --> 00:13:55.583
<i>but in order to run that
pipeline to the aquifer.</i>

237
00:13:55.584 --> 00:13:58.920
<i>you need to get Staten Kirkland
and Cap Fuller on board.</i>

238
00:13:58.921 --> 00:14:01.047
<i>Without them. the
deal is off the table.</i>

239
00:14:01.048 --> 00:14:02.924
Don't worry. I'll get it done.

240
00:14:02.925 --> 00:14:05.301
<i>That second mortgage on your
ranch is depending on it.</i>

241
00:14:05.302 --> 00:14:06.470
Yeah.

242
00:14:15.813 --> 00:14:18.858
- What are you doing?
- Same thing we've been doing for months.

243
00:14:20.234 --> 00:14:22.611
Yeah. but what if Reid sees?

244
00:14:23.153 --> 00:14:24.989
I can take care of myself.

245
00:14:31.412 --> 00:14:32.287
[Lauren moans]

246
00:14:32.288 --> 00:14:33.621
[soft piano music plays]

247
00:14:33.622 --> 00:14:35.373
[both breathing heavily]

248
00:14:35.374 --> 00:14:42.381
[music continues]

249
00:15:21.545 --> 00:15:23.047
[intriguing music plays]

250
00:15:28.636 --> 00:15:29.678
[vehicle approaches]

251
00:15:41.732 --> 00:15:45.903
[police radio chatter]

252
00:15:59.083 --> 00:16:00.792
[officer] Can I help you. son?

253
00:16:00.793 --> 00:16:04.754
Uh. just heading up to the Fuller
Ranch. Got some work lined up there.

254
00:16:04.755 --> 00:16:06.547
- I'll give you a ride.
- [pats seat]

255
00:16:06.548 --> 00:16:07.548
Come on.

256
00:16:12.972 --> 00:16:14.052
- [car door closes]
- Howdy.

257
00:16:14.556 --> 00:16:15.556
Yancy Grey.

258
00:16:15.557 --> 00:16:16.474
Sheriff Brigman.

259
00:16:16.475 --> 00:16:18.477
Welcome to Ransom Canyon. Yancy.

260
00:16:23.691 --> 00:16:25.526
Where'd you say you
were from again?

261
00:16:27.194 --> 00:16:28.194
You know.

262
00:16:28.529 --> 00:16:30.780
Here and there.
No place special.

263
00:16:30.781 --> 00:16:32.700
I take it you worked
a ranch before?

264
00:16:33.325 --> 00:16:35.411
- Yeah.
- Anywhere I'd know?

265
00:16:37.705 --> 00:16:38.705
Uh...

266
00:16:39.123 --> 00:16:40.665
- It...
- Let me guess.

267
00:16:40.666 --> 00:16:42.501
Here and there.
No place special.

268
00:16:46.547 --> 00:16:49.174
[laughs] Relax. just
busting your chops.

269
00:16:49.675 --> 00:16:52.761
Knowing Cap Fuller. you might want
to head back to here and there.

270
00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:56.515
- Why is that?
- I guess you'll find out.

271
00:16:57.016 --> 00:16:59.852
[animated music playing]

272
00:17:10.863 --> 00:17:11.863
[car door closes]

273
00:17:20.289 --> 00:17:21.290
You're late.

274
00:17:22.082 --> 00:17:24.460
- Sorry about that. Yancy Grey.
- Let's go.

275
00:17:25.586 --> 00:17:27.004
[horse whinnies in distance]

276
00:17:31.133 --> 00:17:31.966
[whinnies]

277
00:17:31.967 --> 00:17:33.760
Now the stalls need mucking.

278
00:17:33.761 --> 00:17:36.721
the horses need shoeing.
fences need mending.

279
00:17:36.722 --> 00:17:39.474
Days are long. and we
already agreed on pay.

280
00:17:39.475 --> 00:17:43.103
That is... well. I don't
renegotiate. you got it?

281
00:17:44.229 --> 00:17:46.315
- I'm your man. Mr. Fuller.
- Your new digs.

282
00:17:48.358 --> 00:17:49.358
[horse snorts]

283
00:17:50.778 --> 00:17:52.071
That a problem?

284
00:17:53.614 --> 00:17:54.907
Feels like home already.

285
00:18:01.705 --> 00:18:03.707
["Color You In" by
Yam Haus playing]

286
00:18:07.086 --> 00:18:11.339
<i>♪ Don't think twice
about what this means ♪</i>

287
00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:16.594
<i>♪ It's just a fantasy
Spinning like rotisserie ♪</i>

288
00:18:16.595 --> 00:18:21.974
<i>♪ When we first caught eyes
I was red in the cheeks ♪</i>

289
00:18:21.975 --> 00:18:25.895
<i>♪ You were a canvas
Standing in front of me ♪</i>

290
00:18:25.896 --> 00:18:29.733
<i>♪ I wanna color you in ♪</i>

291
00:18:32.611 --> 00:18:34.321
Morning to you too. Staten.

292
00:18:35.364 --> 00:18:39.200
<i>♪ I wanna color you in ♪</i>

293
00:18:39.201 --> 00:18:40.535
[Quinn] Come on. Biscuit.

294
00:18:40.536 --> 00:18:42.079
[light alternative music fades]

295
00:18:47.167 --> 00:18:48.627
[horses whinnying]

296
00:18:49.586 --> 00:18:50.586
Cap?

297
00:18:51.672 --> 00:18:52.756
You in here?

298
00:19:02.182 --> 00:19:03.724
Just who in the hell are you?

299
00:19:03.725 --> 00:19:05.477
- [bangs]
- [Yancy] Ah! Damn!

300
00:19:08.272 --> 00:19:09.564
I think you'll survive.

301
00:19:09.565 --> 00:19:12.359
- Is that your medical opinion?
- Matter of fact. it is.

302
00:19:12.985 --> 00:19:14.236
I used to be a nurse.

303
00:19:16.613 --> 00:19:18.865
Sorry if I... rattled you.

304
00:19:18.866 --> 00:19:19.950
Don't be.

305
00:19:20.868 --> 00:19:23.537
You didn't. You gonna
tell me who you are now?

306
00:19:24.037 --> 00:19:26.206
- Cap's new foreman.
- Oh right!

307
00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:28.667
- Randy.
- Yancy.

308
00:19:31.044 --> 00:19:32.295
And you are?

309
00:19:32.296 --> 00:19:34.256
Ellie Estevez.

310
00:19:35.174 --> 00:19:39.303
Cap and my pops go way back.
so I pop in. keep an eye out.

311
00:19:39.803 --> 00:19:41.221
do some errands for him.

312
00:19:41.722 --> 00:19:45.474
Actually. would you mind
taking this to the house?

313
00:19:45.475 --> 00:19:48.769
Blood pressure meds. I'm
kinda running late for work.

314
00:19:48.770 --> 00:19:50.564
- Hospital?
- Bar.

315
00:19:51.064 --> 00:19:52.983
Well. dance hall.

316
00:19:54.651 --> 00:19:57.237
You should. um. stop by.

317
00:19:58.197 --> 00:20:00.489
"Welcome to Ransom"
drinks on me.

318
00:20:00.490 --> 00:20:02.075
I just might do that.

319
00:20:05.579 --> 00:20:08.039
It's nice to meet
you. Ellie Estevez.

320
00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:10.125
[soft music playing]

321
00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:21.010
Huh.

322
00:20:21.595 --> 00:20:23.472
Look at you.

323
00:20:32.272 --> 00:20:35.901
[foreboding music playing]

324
00:20:50.499 --> 00:20:51.667
What the hell?

325
00:20:52.876 --> 00:20:54.878
[students chattering]

326
00:20:55.963 --> 00:20:58.003
["Blondie" by Modern Aquatic
playing on truck radio]

327
00:20:58.590 --> 00:20:59.966
Hey. thanks for the ride.

328
00:20:59.967 --> 00:21:03.427
- Don't forget. rent is due today.
- Yeah. yeah. I got it handled.

329
00:21:03.428 --> 00:21:04.930
Keep focusing on
school. all right?

330
00:21:07.266 --> 00:21:08.516
[Lucas groans]

331
00:21:08.517 --> 00:21:09.517
Oh!

332
00:21:10.394 --> 00:21:12.104
- And stay out of trouble. Kit.
- Mm.

333
00:21:18.068 --> 00:21:23.031
<i>♪ And you You try ♪</i>

334
00:21:23.824 --> 00:21:26.909
<i>♪ To work your way back
in to see my life ♪</i>

335
00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:29.412
[laughs] Way to
shoot your shot. bro.

336
00:21:29.413 --> 00:21:32.165
- [class bell rings]
- [upbeat alternative music stops]

337
00:21:33.458 --> 00:21:35.209
- Guess what?
- What?

338
00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:39.088
[laughs] Turns out UT's scout
was at the game after all.

339
00:21:39.089 --> 00:21:40.006
Shut up.

340
00:21:40.007 --> 00:21:42.842
She wants us to come to
Austin for their cheer clinic.

341
00:21:42.843 --> 00:21:45.845
- You know what this could mean?
- It could mean a full ride to UT!

342
00:21:45.846 --> 00:21:48.848
- That's right. We did it. bitch.
- We did it. yeah!

343
00:21:48.849 --> 00:21:51.685
[laughing and screaming]

344
00:21:54.479 --> 00:21:55.479
[Quinn] Oh.

345
00:21:56.315 --> 00:21:58.025
- Would you like some pie?
- Hm.

346
00:22:00.944 --> 00:22:03.446
- Needs a new belt. doesn't it?
- Yep.

347
00:22:03.447 --> 00:22:06.116
- Did I not say it was the belt?
- You did.

348
00:22:06.950 --> 00:22:07.950
And you were right.

349
00:22:09.911 --> 00:22:12.496
Sorry about last night.
Shouldn't have pushed you to go.

350
00:22:12.497 --> 00:22:16.876
No. you didn't... You
didn't push. It's fine.

351
00:22:16.877 --> 00:22:19.337
I just... I guess
I just wanted...

352
00:22:19.338 --> 00:22:20.380
Wanted to what?

353
00:22:22.174 --> 00:22:24.676
What. ease me back into
the world of the living?

354
00:22:25.469 --> 00:22:26.469
Yeah.

355
00:22:26.845 --> 00:22:27.846
I get it.

356
00:22:31.308 --> 00:22:32.601
Oh. I can do that.

357
00:22:33.352 --> 00:22:34.353
Already done.

358
00:22:38.732 --> 00:22:39.732
[water shuts off]

359
00:22:42.486 --> 00:22:45.655
[quiet. emotional music playing]

360
00:22:56.458 --> 00:22:58.710
You used to wear your hair
like that in high school.

361
00:23:01.088 --> 00:23:02.089
Yeah.

362
00:23:07.260 --> 00:23:10.471
Okay. well. I'll figure that belt
out and get back to you tomorrow.

363
00:23:10.472 --> 00:23:11.556
All right.

364
00:23:12.974 --> 00:23:15.142
Yeah. okay. I'll see you then.

365
00:23:15.143 --> 00:23:17.229
[footsteps receding]

366
00:23:19.689 --> 00:23:21.191
[vehicle approaching]

367
00:23:26.530 --> 00:23:27.530
[engine shuts off]

368
00:23:27.864 --> 00:23:28.864
[truck door closes]

369
00:23:30.951 --> 00:23:33.161
I'm gonna need a drink for this.

370
00:23:34.579 --> 00:23:35.579
[Staten exhales]

371
00:23:37.332 --> 00:23:38.834
- [bottle top clinks]
- So...

372
00:23:39.543 --> 00:23:41.753
To what do I owe
the pleasure. Davis?

373
00:23:42.546 --> 00:23:44.422
You're really gonna
make me say it?

374
00:23:44.423 --> 00:23:48.008
Well. I know it's not because you want me
to sell my land to those Austin water boys

375
00:23:48.009 --> 00:23:50.720
so they can build their
damn pipeline. right?

376
00:23:52.264 --> 00:23:53.306
This is my home.

377
00:23:55.058 --> 00:23:56.058
I know.

378
00:23:56.393 --> 00:23:57.936
And it will stay that way.

379
00:23:58.437 --> 00:24:00.396
They'll guarantee a leaseback.

380
00:24:00.397 --> 00:24:01.481
Nothing changes.

381
00:24:02.232 --> 00:24:06.444
Except you. me. and Cap will all
be. uh. several million richer.

382
00:24:06.445 --> 00:24:08.279
Yeah. I don't need
any more money.

383
00:24:08.280 --> 00:24:09.823
[laughing] Yeah.
I know you don't.

384
00:24:10.365 --> 00:24:14.285
But. you know. you inherited
60.000 acres in a trust fund. so...

385
00:24:14.286 --> 00:24:17.414
[laughs] Yeah. well. you're not
doing so bad yourself. are you?

386
00:24:19.749 --> 00:24:20.708
[exhales]

387
00:24:20.709 --> 00:24:21.709
Staten...

388
00:24:22.461 --> 00:24:25.422
This would be good for
Ransom. for the town.

389
00:24:26.256 --> 00:24:29.300
Look. don't be so provincial. Think about
people apart from yourself for once.

390
00:24:29.301 --> 00:24:30.886
You got no goddamn sense.

391
00:24:33.555 --> 00:24:34.973
The world's drying up.

392
00:24:35.515 --> 00:24:38.559
That aquifer feeds our wells.
our crops. and our cattle.

393
00:24:38.560 --> 00:24:41.312
and I'm not gonna let them
run it dry. You understand?

394
00:24:41.313 --> 00:24:42.938
[tense music playing]

395
00:24:42.939 --> 00:24:47.527
Staten. the town has already
granted permission for the pipeline.

396
00:24:49.446 --> 00:24:52.073
It's only a matter of
time until I find a way.

397
00:24:52.574 --> 00:24:55.243
with or without you.

398
00:25:01.291 --> 00:25:02.626
Thanks for the drink.

399
00:25:13.053 --> 00:25:15.055
[distant birds calling]

400
00:25:16.014 --> 00:25:18.016
[horse squealing]

401
00:25:19.059 --> 00:25:20.392
[whinnying]

402
00:25:20.393 --> 00:25:21.937
[snorts]

403
00:25:22.521 --> 00:25:24.146
[Staten whispers] Hey.

404
00:25:24.147 --> 00:25:26.858
It's okay. It's okay.
it's okay. it's okay.

405
00:25:27.526 --> 00:25:29.235
Hey. it's all right.

406
00:25:29.236 --> 00:25:31.279
It's all right.

407
00:25:32.364 --> 00:25:35.909
You gotta be patient. all right?
Breaking a horse takes time.

408
00:25:37.077 --> 00:25:38.328
All right. Come on.

409
00:25:39.037 --> 00:25:40.705
It's okay. It's okay.

410
00:25:47.379 --> 00:25:48.380
Ready. boss?

411
00:25:52.676 --> 00:25:54.678
[wind blowing]

412
00:26:09.484 --> 00:26:10.734
[sighs]

413
00:26:10.735 --> 00:26:12.821
[solemn music playing]

414
00:26:24.666 --> 00:26:25.666
[sniffles]

415
00:26:27.669 --> 00:26:29.671
[quietly sobbing]

416
00:26:52.569 --> 00:26:54.571
[mysterious music playing]

417
00:27:07.584 --> 00:27:09.085
[Jake] What you
got there. Staten?

418
00:27:11.212 --> 00:27:12.255
An answer.

419
00:27:21.389 --> 00:27:23.015
Who the hell's that?

420
00:27:23.016 --> 00:27:26.518
Looks like Austin Water & Power
surveying for the pipeline again.

421
00:27:26.519 --> 00:27:27.687
God damn it.

422
00:27:28.855 --> 00:27:32.066
All right. you tell them that
this is private property.

423
00:27:32.067 --> 00:27:35.695
If they don't leave. you shoot 'em.
Kidding. Just... Just get rid of 'em.

424
00:27:48.333 --> 00:27:49.584
[Staten] There it is.

425
00:27:50.752 --> 00:27:51.961
There's your proof.

426
00:27:53.213 --> 00:27:54.255
Proof of what exactly?

427
00:27:55.131 --> 00:27:57.592
Proof there was another
car on the road that night.

428
00:27:58.718 --> 00:27:59.551
[sighs]

429
00:27:59.552 --> 00:28:02.138
Dan. I'm... Listen.
I'm telling you.

430
00:28:03.890 --> 00:28:05.308
Somebody else made him crash.

431
00:28:06.142 --> 00:28:09.186
Look. I know this is hard.
today being a year and all.

432
00:28:09.187 --> 00:28:12.107
But your boy was alone out there
that night. You understand?

433
00:28:13.400 --> 00:28:14.776
You gotta let this theory go.

434
00:28:17.654 --> 00:28:18.654
Staten...

435
00:28:19.572 --> 00:28:22.408
Hey. [sighs] Have you
thought about taking a break?

436
00:28:22.409 --> 00:28:24.243
Maybe giving yourself
a little vacation?

437
00:28:24.244 --> 00:28:27.371
Well. I'm just saying it
might do you some good.

438
00:28:27.372 --> 00:28:29.249
Might... Might do me some good?

439
00:28:30.166 --> 00:28:33.878
You know what would do me some good.
Dan. is if you did your goddamn job.

440
00:28:37.006 --> 00:28:39.008
[footsteps receding]

441
00:28:39.884 --> 00:28:42.011
Why do you let him talk
to you like that. Sheriff?

442
00:28:44.139 --> 00:28:47.225
Well. because that man has
lost everything he loves. Kai.

443
00:28:48.727 --> 00:28:50.645
And he's looking for a reason.

444
00:28:51.479 --> 00:28:53.022
Even if there isn't one.

445
00:28:53.648 --> 00:28:55.650
[pensive music playing]

446
00:29:09.205 --> 00:29:11.416
[mechanical creaking]

447
00:29:13.376 --> 00:29:15.420
[machinery clicking
and creaking]

448
00:29:16.463 --> 00:29:17.964
- [creaking]
- [Staten grunts]

449
00:29:19.716 --> 00:29:21.426
[creaking continues]

450
00:29:22.469 --> 00:29:24.137
- [mechanism bangs]
- [Staten exclaims]

451
00:29:25.263 --> 00:29:26.138
[frustrated groan]

452
00:29:26.139 --> 00:29:27.724
[Quinn] Want me to get in there?

453
00:29:28.808 --> 00:29:29.934
Smaller hands.

454
00:29:31.102 --> 00:29:32.353
No. I'll get it.

455
00:29:38.276 --> 00:29:40.278
[ratchet clicking]

456
00:29:41.571 --> 00:29:43.031
[Staten panting]

457
00:29:47.076 --> 00:29:47.910
[grunts]

458
00:29:47.911 --> 00:29:49.370
Hey.

459
00:29:50.789 --> 00:29:51.790
Talk to me.

460
00:29:54.334 --> 00:29:55.376
I'm good.

461
00:29:57.170 --> 00:29:59.172
[continues ratcheting]

462
00:30:01.299 --> 00:30:03.301
Would you just let
me fix the damn belt?

463
00:30:04.844 --> 00:30:07.263
Yeah. you know what?
Have at it. Staten.

464
00:30:07.764 --> 00:30:09.766
[pensive music plays]

465
00:30:28.409 --> 00:30:31.788
[class bell rings]

466
00:30:33.039 --> 00:30:35.290
[Lauren] My mom's a drunk. and
I'm the one who has to stay.

467
00:30:35.291 --> 00:30:38.335
Oh come on. Your dad wouldn't make
you give up a full ride at UT.

468
00:30:38.336 --> 00:30:39.420
Well. he did.

469
00:30:40.380 --> 00:30:44.342
He doesn't realize being stuck here
is what made my mom the way she is.

470
00:30:47.136 --> 00:30:49.347
I just don't want
to end up like her.

471
00:30:50.473 --> 00:30:51.473
I won't.

472
00:30:51.808 --> 00:30:52.851
Hey.

473
00:30:55.228 --> 00:30:56.813
I'm not gonna let that happen.

474
00:31:00.650 --> 00:31:03.194
[serious music playing]

475
00:31:12.787 --> 00:31:15.123
[horse whinnies]

476
00:31:15.665 --> 00:31:17.959
Not gonna use the power sander?

477
00:31:19.711 --> 00:31:21.462
- You got a power sander?
- Yup.

478
00:31:23.673 --> 00:31:26.925
Might have been. uh. helpful to
let me know before I started.

479
00:31:26.926 --> 00:31:29.595
Well. I'm not one
to micromanage.

480
00:31:29.596 --> 00:31:32.181
[vehicle approaching]

481
00:31:34.726 --> 00:31:35.976
[truck door opens]

482
00:31:35.977 --> 00:31:36.977
[door closes]

483
00:31:38.021 --> 00:31:39.104
Don't get up.

484
00:31:39.105 --> 00:31:40.939
I know how hard that
is for you these days.

485
00:31:40.940 --> 00:31:41.983
[Cap groans]

486
00:31:42.483 --> 00:31:45.569
Couple years ago. I'd have
whooped your ass bad for that.

487
00:31:45.570 --> 00:31:48.447
- Think we both know you still could.
- You want a beer?

488
00:31:48.448 --> 00:31:50.908
No. no. I'm set. How
you doing. old boy?

489
00:31:50.909 --> 00:31:51.867
Eh.

490
00:31:51.868 --> 00:31:55.746
You... getting
charitable over here?

491
00:31:55.747 --> 00:31:58.040
We'll see how long he lasts.

492
00:31:58.041 --> 00:32:00.042
What's eating at you?

493
00:32:00.043 --> 00:32:01.085
[sighs]

494
00:32:02.337 --> 00:32:04.504
- Austin Water & Power.
- Oh.

495
00:32:04.505 --> 00:32:06.673
They been dripping
honey in your ear too?

496
00:32:06.674 --> 00:32:07.966
They're trying to.

497
00:32:07.967 --> 00:32:11.845
Davis came by. wants me
to sit down with 'em.

498
00:32:11.846 --> 00:32:14.181
I think we need to
lock arms on this. Cap.

499
00:32:14.182 --> 00:32:17.434
Let me talk to the utilities commission
and have them run some oversight.

500
00:32:17.435 --> 00:32:19.728
The numbers they're batting
around ain't nothing.

501
00:32:19.729 --> 00:32:21.396
Yeah. I know the
numbers. all right?

502
00:32:21.397 --> 00:32:23.483
But these are our homes
we're talking about.

503
00:32:24.192 --> 00:32:25.902
These ranches are our legacy.

504
00:32:27.362 --> 00:32:28.696
Legacy to who?

505
00:32:29.489 --> 00:32:30.865
Our sons are dead.

506
00:32:40.041 --> 00:32:42.418
[muffled music playing]

507
00:32:51.260 --> 00:32:52.679
What can I get you?

508
00:32:54.138 --> 00:32:55.223
Shiner'd be nice.

509
00:33:04.315 --> 00:33:05.955
- [aggressive thud]
- [bottlecap clatters]

510
00:33:10.530 --> 00:33:11.697
Did I miss something here?

511
00:33:11.698 --> 00:33:14.283
I saw that article
in your little book.

512
00:33:14.993 --> 00:33:16.284
I care about Cap.

513
00:33:16.285 --> 00:33:20.455
You could work at half a dozen
ranches for twice the pay.

514
00:33:20.456 --> 00:33:22.874
It just didn't make any
sense. And then I...

515
00:33:22.875 --> 00:33:24.961
And then you thought
the worst. I get it.

516
00:33:26.004 --> 00:33:30.717
Look. far as other ranches are concerned.
the last place I was at didn't go so well.

517
00:33:31.217 --> 00:33:33.886
Cap was the only one that
didn't ask for references.

518
00:33:34.387 --> 00:33:35.638
As far as that paper.

519
00:33:36.139 --> 00:33:38.265
I was just trying to see
what his place used to be.

520
00:33:38.266 --> 00:33:39.892
see if I could
help bring it back.

521
00:33:41.352 --> 00:33:42.353
And that's it?

522
00:33:43.271 --> 00:33:44.271
That's it.

523
00:33:48.901 --> 00:33:51.237
You so much as cross
that old man...

524
00:33:52.530 --> 00:33:54.282
I will see to it you suffer.

525
00:33:58.870 --> 00:33:59.996
Yes. ma'am.

526
00:34:01.330 --> 00:34:02.330
[rap music playing]

527
00:34:02.331 --> 00:34:03.832
<i>♪ Bad energy don't
suit the fella ♪</i>

528
00:34:03.833 --> 00:34:05.292
<i>♪ Dunno why I keep that fruit ♪</i>

529
00:34:05.293 --> 00:34:07.878
<i>♪ Better calm down They
super jealous. over-zealous ♪</i>

530
00:34:07.879 --> 00:34:08.795
Cheers!

531
00:34:08.796 --> 00:34:11.340
<i>♪ We celebrate for the hell
of it. got champagne pop... ♪</i>

532
00:34:15.887 --> 00:34:17.013
Yo. uh. Lucas.

533
00:34:18.347 --> 00:34:20.308
When are you gonna come
work for my dad. man?

534
00:34:21.225 --> 00:34:24.144
- What?
- I mean. like. your brother's there now.

535
00:34:24.145 --> 00:34:26.564
You know. your old man
was there back in the day.

536
00:34:27.231 --> 00:34:30.860
Just a regular Russell
family tradition.

537
00:34:31.444 --> 00:34:32.570
Yeah. I guess so.

538
00:34:35.740 --> 00:34:37.867
Your dad taught me how
to ride when I was a kid.

539
00:34:41.079 --> 00:34:43.414
- I didn't know that.
- He was a hell of a wrangler too.

540
00:34:44.999 --> 00:34:46.000
That he was.

541
00:34:46.501 --> 00:34:48.711
[music continues]

542
00:35:04.060 --> 00:35:05.061
Hey.

543
00:35:05.686 --> 00:35:08.730
- What are y'all doing up here?
- [Reid] You're just in time.

544
00:35:08.731 --> 00:35:11.275
I was about to clear
something up with Lucas here.

545
00:35:13.277 --> 00:35:15.779
You need to leave
my woman alone.

546
00:35:15.780 --> 00:35:17.281
- Oh my God.
- [Lucas] Uh...

547
00:35:17.865 --> 00:35:20.659
I'm sorry. I think I'm mistaken.
Do we have a problem here?

548
00:35:20.660 --> 00:35:23.246
You gotta be kidding me with
this toxic male whatever this is.

549
00:35:23.830 --> 00:35:25.748
Really? Lucas. let's go.

550
00:35:26.707 --> 00:35:27.707
Come on.

551
00:35:30.086 --> 00:35:30.961
[ominous music plays]

552
00:35:30.962 --> 00:35:32.420
- [police siren blares]
- [boy] Cops!

553
00:35:32.421 --> 00:35:33.755
Yo. check it out. check it out!

554
00:35:33.756 --> 00:35:37.802
- [teens clamoring]
- [boy] No. no!

555
00:35:42.431 --> 00:35:44.851
[car engines revving. leaving]

556
00:35:49.313 --> 00:35:52.065
Oh God. Did any
of you guys drive?

557
00:35:52.066 --> 00:35:53.608
- No.
- Ben was designated.

558
00:35:53.609 --> 00:35:55.153
I don't have a car.

559
00:35:55.987 --> 00:35:56.987
Great.

560
00:35:58.072 --> 00:35:59.073
Okay. well...

561
00:36:00.032 --> 00:36:02.994
Yeah. we have no service
either. so we're stranded.

562
00:36:03.703 --> 00:36:04.954
[Lauren sighs]

563
00:36:06.164 --> 00:36:08.373
- Whoa.
- Hey. how is this my fault?

564
00:36:08.374 --> 00:36:10.014
- [Lauren] Let's go.
- [Reid] What'd I do?

565
00:36:13.921 --> 00:36:15.548
You were not at that show.

566
00:36:16.257 --> 00:36:18.842
Rampart Theater. back
row. I swear to God.

567
00:36:18.843 --> 00:36:21.011
[laughs] You are full of it.

568
00:36:21.012 --> 00:36:23.556
[laughs] Okay. listen.

569
00:36:24.807 --> 00:36:26.141
I was at school.

570
00:36:26.142 --> 00:36:29.269
Amalah told me that you
had a showcase concert.

571
00:36:29.270 --> 00:36:30.437
Mm-hmm.

572
00:36:30.438 --> 00:36:33.816
So I went into the city
and I. uh. saw you play.

573
00:36:34.358 --> 00:36:36.652
You were... You
were unbelievable.

574
00:36:37.403 --> 00:36:38.613
[laughs]

575
00:36:39.655 --> 00:36:42.866
Okay. in case it hasn't
been abundantly clear.

576
00:36:42.867 --> 00:36:45.453
I've had a thing for you
since... since forever.

577
00:36:46.204 --> 00:36:48.580
Look. I... I was always
worried that you. um...

578
00:36:48.581 --> 00:36:51.208
You know. you wouldn't
see me as anything more

579
00:36:51.209 --> 00:36:55.670
than your best friend's little brother
who was utterly infatuated with you.

580
00:36:55.671 --> 00:37:00.593
And yet you've been utterly
infatuated before. Mr. Collins.

581
00:37:02.178 --> 00:37:03.053
I was at your wedding.

582
00:37:03.054 --> 00:37:04.763
- [laughs]
- Both of them.

583
00:37:04.764 --> 00:37:07.183
Whatever happened to Miss Texas?

584
00:37:09.894 --> 00:37:11.687
- It's complicated.
- Ah. okay.

585
00:37:14.941 --> 00:37:18.152
So... [clears throat]
Why didn't you go back?

586
00:37:18.736 --> 00:37:21.405
When Amalah got sick and
you came home from New York?

587
00:37:22.448 --> 00:37:23.991
Why didn't you go back?

588
00:37:27.078 --> 00:37:27.953
[door opens]

589
00:37:27.954 --> 00:37:29.288
It's complicated.

590
00:37:31.374 --> 00:37:32.375
[door closes]

591
00:37:32.875 --> 00:37:34.210
[footsteps approach]

592
00:37:34.752 --> 00:37:36.920
[Staten] Hey. June.
I'm here to pick up.

593
00:37:36.921 --> 00:37:38.046
[June] Coming right up.

594
00:37:38.047 --> 00:37:39.131
Thank you.

595
00:37:50.851 --> 00:37:53.311
Tell your buddies at Austin
Water & Power to stop calling.

596
00:37:53.312 --> 00:37:54.981
because I'm not
selling. You understand?

597
00:38:02.196 --> 00:38:03.780
Yeah. uh. sorry about that.

598
00:38:03.781 --> 00:38:05.866
[apprehensive music playing]

599
00:38:13.749 --> 00:38:14.749
Well...

600
00:38:16.419 --> 00:38:17.837
[somber music plays]

601
00:38:28.431 --> 00:38:32.351
[thunder rumbles]

602
00:38:33.602 --> 00:38:35.521
What the hell is she
doing with Davis?

603
00:38:36.731 --> 00:38:38.149
Oh my God.

604
00:38:41.902 --> 00:38:43.278
[Lauren] Please. be quiet!

605
00:38:43.279 --> 00:38:44.946
[Lucas] Oh hey! Hey!

606
00:38:44.947 --> 00:38:46.866
[all] Hey!

607
00:38:48.409 --> 00:38:50.828
And the Darwin Award goes to...

608
00:38:53.497 --> 00:38:57.208
[thunder crashing]

609
00:38:57.209 --> 00:38:59.670
All right. There. Let's
take cover over there.

610
00:39:00.254 --> 00:39:01.463
Ghost house? No way. man.

611
00:39:01.464 --> 00:39:03.340
Fine. Freeze.

612
00:39:03.341 --> 00:39:04.508
[wind blowing]

613
00:39:05.092 --> 00:39:06.092
[frustrated growl]

614
00:39:07.636 --> 00:39:10.848
[thunder continues]

615
00:39:16.228 --> 00:39:17.396
[door slams]

616
00:39:18.314 --> 00:39:20.190
- [thunder crashes]
- [Lauren gasps]

617
00:39:20.191 --> 00:39:21.399
[Lauren] Guys...

618
00:39:21.400 --> 00:39:23.318
Reid. I don't have a
good feeling about this.

619
00:39:23.319 --> 00:39:24.319
[floor creaks. snaps]

620
00:39:24.320 --> 00:39:26.072
This floor isn't stable.

621
00:39:27.156 --> 00:39:28.114
[floorboard creaks]

622
00:39:28.115 --> 00:39:29.115
Hey. stop.

623
00:39:29.116 --> 00:39:30.950
- It's gonna be fine.
- [Tim] Don't. man.

624
00:39:30.951 --> 00:39:32.202
- What?
- [Lauren] Reid. stop.

625
00:39:32.203 --> 00:39:33.244
- Reid. no!
- [crashing]

626
00:39:33.245 --> 00:39:34.245
[Lucas and Reid yell]

627
00:39:34.246 --> 00:39:35.456
- [Lauren gasps]
- Oh God.

628
00:39:37.166 --> 00:39:38.918
- Over there!
- [boy] My leg!

629
00:39:40.419 --> 00:39:42.421
[boy groans]

630
00:39:42.922 --> 00:39:44.214
[floorboards crumbling]

631
00:39:44.215 --> 00:39:45.341
[Lucas] Lauren. come on.

632
00:39:45.925 --> 00:39:47.092
[thunder rumbles]

633
00:39:47.093 --> 00:39:48.009
Lauren?

634
00:39:48.010 --> 00:39:49.969
[panicked breathing]

635
00:39:49.970 --> 00:39:51.847
- [boy moans]
- [floorboards crumble]

636
00:39:52.640 --> 00:39:54.182
Look at me. Walk to me.

637
00:39:54.183 --> 00:39:55.601
I can't move. I can't move.

638
00:39:58.145 --> 00:39:59.980
[clattering]

639
00:40:02.483 --> 00:40:04.025
Don't... Don't let me fall.

640
00:40:04.026 --> 00:40:05.110
[Lucas] I won't.

641
00:40:05.111 --> 00:40:06.362
[Lauren gasping]

642
00:40:08.656 --> 00:40:10.032
I've got you.

643
00:40:11.200 --> 00:40:13.494
I got you. Come on.

644
00:40:14.286 --> 00:40:15.578
[grunting]

645
00:40:15.579 --> 00:40:16.664
Tim?

646
00:40:20.543 --> 00:40:21.544
Tim!

647
00:40:24.213 --> 00:40:25.214
Oh God.

648
00:40:26.674 --> 00:40:28.217
[grunting]

649
00:40:38.644 --> 00:40:40.187
[panting. groaning]

650
00:40:41.021 --> 00:40:42.021
[Staten] Come on.

651
00:40:42.022 --> 00:40:43.524
Ah!

652
00:40:44.900 --> 00:40:45.985
[Staten] You guys stay put.

653
00:40:46.610 --> 00:40:47.944
Sheriff's on his way.

654
00:40:47.945 --> 00:40:49.655
[Tim groans]

655
00:40:53.742 --> 00:40:54.742
[police radio chattering]

656
00:40:54.743 --> 00:40:57.328
[Reid] Look. all right. I could
tell the floor was unsafe.

657
00:40:57.329 --> 00:40:59.915
And I tried to get 'em to stop
horsing around over there.

658
00:41:00.499 --> 00:41:02.959
They didn't. And then
the floor gave out.

659
00:41:02.960 --> 00:41:03.960
Nuh-uh.

660
00:41:04.545 --> 00:41:07.673
- No. I'm gonna tell him the truth.
- Let's let him play the hero.

661
00:41:08.549 --> 00:41:10.425
But. Lucas. this is
just wrong. Like...

662
00:41:10.426 --> 00:41:11.635
You know the truth.

663
00:41:12.428 --> 00:41:14.138
That's all that matters to me.

664
00:41:16.557 --> 00:41:19.560
[vehicle approaching]

665
00:41:22.146 --> 00:41:23.271
[whispers] Is that your dad?

666
00:41:23.272 --> 00:41:25.191
- [door opens and closes]
- Oh shit!

667
00:41:26.317 --> 00:41:29.235
Dad. listen. I'm fine. okay?
Give me a minute to explain...

668
00:41:29.236 --> 00:41:30.321
Not right now.

669
00:41:30.905 --> 00:41:34.185
I'm still mentally composing the lecture
I'm gonna be giving you the next 10 years.

670
00:41:37.077 --> 00:41:40.122
- Let's go.
- [dispatcher] <i>3-1. what's your 20?</i>

671
00:41:46.212 --> 00:41:48.422
<i>Sarge. this is 4-9 Charlie...</i>

672
00:41:49.757 --> 00:41:51.841
I'm gonna say this
once and only once.

673
00:41:51.842 --> 00:41:53.134
You stay away from that boy.

674
00:41:53.135 --> 00:41:55.762
- That Russell family is trouble.
- But. Dad. you don't understand...

675
00:41:55.763 --> 00:41:57.097
It's not up for discussion.

676
00:41:57.640 --> 00:42:00.016
Now. I am willing to
reconsider that cheer clinic.

677
00:42:00.017 --> 00:42:02.603
at least for now. but this...

678
00:42:03.479 --> 00:42:04.980
this is my one condition.

679
00:42:10.152 --> 00:42:11.862
[somber music playing]

680
00:42:30.798 --> 00:42:33.758
- Hey. Don't worry. Your nephew's okay.
- What happened?

681
00:42:33.759 --> 00:42:35.761
Ah. he's banged up.

682
00:42:36.428 --> 00:42:39.430
Broken legs and busted ribs.
but he's gonna be fine.

683
00:42:39.431 --> 00:42:40.807
Your sister's in there now.

684
00:42:40.808 --> 00:42:41.892
Thank you.

685
00:42:42.810 --> 00:42:44.311
So. Davis. huh?

686
00:42:49.733 --> 00:42:51.569
Now's not really the best time.

687
00:42:53.070 --> 00:42:54.070
All right.

688
00:42:56.156 --> 00:42:57.741
You're unbelievable.
you know that?

689
00:43:01.412 --> 00:43:04.163
You've had a piece of my heart
for as long as I can remember.

690
00:43:04.164 --> 00:43:05.999
- Hold on. What are...
- Listen.

691
00:43:06.000 --> 00:43:08.252
I buried it when you and
Amalah started dating.

692
00:43:09.545 --> 00:43:12.006
Buried it even more when
you two got married.

693
00:43:13.340 --> 00:43:16.552
I moved halfway across
the country to avoid it.

694
00:43:17.052 --> 00:43:19.346
["Hold Me Steady"
by Ronen playing]

695
00:43:22.141 --> 00:43:24.935
When she got sick. I was
here for her and you.

696
00:43:26.312 --> 00:43:29.565
And I've been here ever
since. through all of it.

697
00:43:31.233 --> 00:43:32.359
Through the pain.

698
00:43:34.111 --> 00:43:35.112
the grief.

699
00:43:38.032 --> 00:43:39.158
Through Randall.

700
00:43:42.995 --> 00:43:44.705
And I've waited.

701
00:43:45.956 --> 00:43:47.916
I've waited for you to heal...

702
00:43:50.878 --> 00:43:52.046
to choose me.

703
00:43:54.089 --> 00:43:56.467
But you're never gonna
do that. are you?

704
00:44:00.721 --> 00:44:01.722
Quinn. I...

705
00:44:09.855 --> 00:44:11.607
Why do you care what I do?

706
00:44:17.613 --> 00:44:18.739
I don't.

707
00:44:19.990 --> 00:44:26.955
<i>♪ Hold me steady It's
all so heavy sometimes ♪</i>

708
00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:31.543
<i>♪ Whoa ♪</i>

709
00:44:35.964 --> 00:44:38.592
<i>♪ Hold me steady ♪</i>

710
00:44:43.013 --> 00:44:44.181
Damn it.

711
00:44:46.684 --> 00:44:50.479
<i>♪ Hold me steady ♪</i>

712
00:44:57.361 --> 00:45:00.154
<i>♪ Hold me steady ♪</i>

713
00:45:00.155 --> 00:45:02.241
[gentle piano music fades]

714
00:45:15.587 --> 00:45:16.421
[lighter flicks]

715
00:45:16.422 --> 00:45:19.049
- [vehicle approaches]
- [lighter shuts]

716
00:45:35.274 --> 00:45:36.734
All's going to plan with Cap.

717
00:45:37.609 --> 00:45:39.527
But you didn't tell
me about the girl.

718
00:45:39.528 --> 00:45:41.113
[soft. dramatic music playing]

719
00:45:41.947 --> 00:45:42.948
Does it matter?

720
00:45:48.495 --> 00:45:49.955
We're sure about this?

721
00:45:51.415 --> 00:45:55.002
'Cause once you go through
with it. there's no going back.

722
00:45:58.005 --> 00:45:59.423
That's what I'm counting on.

723
00:46:11.268 --> 00:46:13.729
[soft. pensive music playing]

724
00:48:53.472 --> 00:48:55.015
[music fades]

724
00:48:56.305 --> 00:49:56.199
Do you want subtitles for any video?
